   "text": {
    "L1": "A nonsense poem is meant to make us laugh, not to make perfect sense.",
    "L2": "That is why calling it a bad poem is a mistake.",
    "L3": "The funny man wears shoes on his ears and eats soup with a banana.",
    "L4": "These impossible, upside-down actions surprise us, and the surprise makes us laugh.",
    "L5": "A rhyme scheme shows the pattern of rhyming line endings with letters.",
    "L6": "Ludhiana rhymes with banana, and ears rhymes with years, so the pattern is ABAB.",
    "L7": "When an adverb describes an action, say, “He laughed loudly” or “He danced well.”",
    "L8": "Now choose the rhyme scheme of the four-line stanza."
   },
